  "status": "ok",
  "summary_en": "Grunge Rusty Surface generates a layered-noise pattern imitating a rusty surface, with controls for rust intensity, variation and corrosion lines. It is meant as a mask or building block for detailed textures, such as metal roofs or vehicle parts.",
  "inputs": [
    "size_ref: representative layer that sets the output size and metadata"
  ],
  "key_parameters": [
    "Amplitude: multiplies values (originally 0 to 1) before Center",
    "Center: offsets the output values",
    "Mask Contrast: adjusts contrast before Amplitude and Center",
    "Element Size, Offset, Tile Size: pattern scale, position and repeat period",
    "Primary Roughness: horizontal distortion along Y, giving rougher edges and waves",
    "Secondary Roughness: vertical distortion along X, with similar effects",
    "Cracks Mask: visibility of the vertical crack lines; higher values darken and reveal them",
    "Cracks Size: crack scale relative to Element Size; higher values give fewer, larger cracks",
    "Seed: changes the random variation while keeping the look",
    "Post Processing, applied in order: Fold, Complement, Bias, Gain, Gamma, Contrast, Clamp Minimum, Clamp Maximum"
  ],
  "caveats": [
    "Amplitude and Center can produce values below 0 or above 1; use the Clamp options",
    "Complement assumes values from 0 to 1",
    "Fold has no visible effect when all values are positive",
    "Post-processing Contrast differs from Noise Contrast on some noise nodes"
  ],
  "resume_fr": "Grunge Rusty Surface imite une surface rouillée avec ses bords irréguliers et ses fissures de corrosion, utilisable en masque pour une toiture ou une pièce de véhicule."
}
